From 56984640e1d9ce587f83dff975a37812a5741064 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Sam (local build)" <sam@local>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:30:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] dde-emu: firmware (PICO_FLEXRAY_DDE_EMU=ON): transmit DDE
 static frames on FR1

New build option, default OFF (stock build unchanged). With it ON:
FR1 streamer + timestamp marks only, no forwarder, FR2 TX held off.
pio0 dde_emu_tx/dde_emu_fire send a prepared frame at a 10 ns PWM-tick
deadline computed from the car's own reference frames; TIMER0 alarm on
core1 at IRQ prio 0 arms it. Echo of our own frames calibrates fire
latency and loop delay. TX off at boot; USB 0xa3 enables (wValue 1) /
disables (0) with 20 s keepalive, 0xa4 reads stats. Safety: no TX
without lock, 8 quiet cycles after enable, latched faults on stuck TX,
foreign frame in our slot or 8 missed echoes. Options: EMU_SYNC_BITS
(default 0, unsafe/untested), EMU_DYN_5C (default 0, dynamic 0x5C),
EMU_TSS_BITS (default 7).
